  },
  "decisions": [
    "Default features disabled on all direct SDK and bridge dependencies; official OTLP HTTP/JSON encoder with the existing verified Rustls/Hyper transport.",
    "No reqwest, native TLS, compression, gRPC exporter or internal-logs features. The official HTTP/JSON dependency necessarily enables SDK metrics support transitively; no SDK metric provider replaces the existing registry.",
    "SDK constructors may read ambient defaults internally. Explicit provider resources and sampler/limits replace those defaults; the HTTP adapter discards all SDK destinations and headers and uses only checked file configuration. No process environment mutation.",
    "Effective resource attributes are exactly service.name, service.version and opaque service.instance.id.",
    "First-party bounded processors expose queue loss and deadlines; official SDK log/span models and codecs remain the wire authority."
  ],
